*     LABEL                                                             TD  0000
*       DUMP                                                            TD  0001
*      FAP                                                              TD  0002
*        IMPROVED TAPE DUMP  ---   TREVOR BARKER                        TD  0003
*       AUGUST 21,1958                                                  TD  0004
*     INPUT -- TAPE ADDRESS IN TOP ROW OF KEYS                          TD  0005
*     POSITIONING -- SW5 DOWN TO REWIND                                 TD  0006
*          DIVIDE LOWER KEYS INTO TWO SETS OF NINE, CONSIDER EACH AS    TD  0007
*          A SIGNED 8 BIT NUMBER.   THE FIRST IS THE NUMBER OF FILES TO TD  0008
*          MOVE, THE SECOND RECORDS (+ FOR FORWARDS, - FOR BACK)        TD  0009
*     OUTPUT -- SW1 UP TO PRINT ONLINE, SW2 DOWN TO PREPARE TAPE A2     TD  0010
*          FOR OFFLINE PRINTER (NOT ON PROGRAM CONTROL)                 TD  0011
*     STOP -- SW4 DOWN TO STOP AT ANY TIME.                             TD  0012
*          IF THE LEFTMOST SIX KEYS OF THE TOP ROW ARE NOT ZERO,        TD  0013
*          PROGRAM WILL STOP AFTER THIS MANY FILES                      TD  0014
*     DECIMAL OUTPUT -- SW3 DOWN TO PRINT BINARY RECORDS IN DECIMAL     TD  0015
*          INSTEAD OF OCTAL                                             TD  0016
*     SW6 DOWN TO FORCE BINARY STYLE PRINTING (OCTAL OR                 TD  0017
*          DECIMAL)  FOR BCD RECORDS                                    TD  0018
       ENTRY   TDUMP         AC NON ZERO                                TD  0019
ORG    OPSYN   NULL                                                     TD  0020
ABS    OPSYN   NULL                                                     TD  0021
...    SYN     0               USED TO INITIALIZE FROM LENGTH           TD  0022
       ORG     0                                                        TD  0023
